{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1786210152,"nonce":"lm9p/i3CnaAmHPUTZzZmrGqThY4=","target":"344bf683e7f7f9f642f14000452b04993842d2c8ca11c256f5ca39a65497153f","message":"**What is wrong.** The retention defaults — raw alerts 14 days, events 13 months —\nare not traceable to any stated requirement.\n`docs/ORCHESTRATION.md:147-149` records them as an open question for the owner:\n\"Regulated buyers needing years would make cold-storage export a v1 requirement.\"\nRetention is now a per-org setting with enforced bounds (commit `a827f4a`), but\nthe numbers themselves remain unvalidated, and there is no export path.\n\n**Why it matters.** oto's entire pitch is \"for every alert that has ever fired\".\n14 days is not \"ever\", and the first buyer who needs a year of history for an\naudit discovers the data was deleted by a default nobody chose deliberately. That\nis unrecoverable — unlike almost every other defect in this backlog, this one\ndestroys the data the product exists to hold. 13 months for events versus 14 days\nfor raw also implies a specific answer about what is reconstructible from which,\nand that answer is not written down anywhere.\n\n**Where.** `internal/identity/domain/settings.go` (retention bounds), the\nretention/reaper jobs, `docs/ORCHESTRATION.md:147-149`,\n`docs/design/SPEC.md` retention sections.\n\n**Done when.** Each default is justified in writing against a real requirement,\nthe docs state plainly what is lost at each boundary and what remains\nreconstructible, and either cold-storage export is scoped as work or the product\nstates that it does not have one. Blocked on the owner.","files":null}]}